# The instruction texts under src/prompt are embedded into the binary exactly as
# the checkout wrote them (`rust_embed`), and the pipeline splits several of them
# on a `---` line so each parallel agent gets its own variant. A checkout that
# rewrites line endings — Windows, where `core.autocrlf` is on by default — would
# ship bytes the repository does not hold and collapse those variants into one.
# LF is therefore pinned for the files below; the rest of the repository is
# unaffected, raw-byte files included.
/src/prompt/** text eol=lf

# The document kit's sources and the bundle built from them follow the same rule,
# for the same reason: the bundle is embedded with `include_bytes!`, and its
# header records a hash of the four sources (assets/docgen/kit.js, rules.json,
# package.json, bun.lock) that a test recomputes from the checkout — a rewrite
# of any of those line endings would change the embedded bytes and break the
# guard. The bundle itself is a generated artifact, so git must not touch it at
# all, on either side of a checkout.
/assets/docgen/kit.js text eol=lf
/assets/docgen/rules.json text eol=lf
/assets/docgen/package.json text eol=lf
/assets/docgen/bun.lock text eol=lf
/assets/docgen/document-kit.js -text
